       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for adults in a monitored setting is 3,200 mg/day, and the OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It adds toxicity risk without adding analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nWas this a typo? These are the common options:\n- 400 mg PO every 6 hours (1,600 mg/day) for mild to moderate pain\n- 600 mg PO every 6 hours (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day), or four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you meant 1,600 mg per day total, I can enter 400 mg four times daily. Tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want the original dose, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I would still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
